Dialogue: 0,0:00:07.45,0:00:09.26,OP,,0,0,0,,{\blur0.6\c&H000000&}I think it's time to blow this scene
Dialogue: 1,0:00:07.45,0:00:09.26,OP,,0,0,0,,{\bord0\blur0.6\shad2\4a&HFF&}I think it's time to blow this scene
Dialogue: 0,0:00:09.26,0:00:11.26,OP,,0,0,0,,{\blur0.6\c&H000000&}Get everybody and their stuff together
Dialogue: 1,0:00:09.26,0:00:11.26,OP,,0,0,0,,{\bord0\blur0.6\shad2\4a&HFF&}Get everybody and their stuff together
Dialogue: 0,0:00:11.26,0:00:13.67,OP,,0,0,0,,{\blur0.6\c&H000000&}Okay, three, two, one let's jam
Dialogue: 1,0:00:11.26,0:00:13.67,OP,,0,0,0,,{\bord0\blur0.6\shad2\4a&HFF&}Okay, three, two, one let's jam
Dialogue: 0,0:01:57.34,0:02:01.22,Default,,0,0,0,,Nothing lasts forever.\NAll things must come to an end.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:01.22,0:02:03.77,Default,,0,0,0,,That is the so called way of nature.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:03.77,0:02:06.39,Default,,0,0,0,,It's rather sudden,\Nbut today is the last episode.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:06.39,0:02:07.88,Default,,0,0,0,,So at this time,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:07.88,0:02:10.56,Default,,0,0,0,,I would like to remember all the things\Nthat have happened and think about them.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:16.32,0:02:20.32,Default,,0,0,0,,Collection Blues
Dialogue: 0,0:02:24.49,0:02:26.50,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm starving...
Dialogue: 0,0:02:29.37,0:02:31.68,Default,,0,0,0,,You too?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:31.68,0:02:35.13,Default,,0,0,0,,"Food For Thought"
Dialogue: 0,0:02:40.89,0:02:42.72,Default,,0,0,0,,Food is very important.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:42.72,0:02:45.92,Default,,0,0,0,,After all, you are what you eat.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:45.92,0:02:48.66,Default,,0,0,0,,Suppose there was a human clone of me
Dialogue: 0,0:02:48.66,0:02:51.73,Default,,0,0,0,,and he had never eaten\Nanything other than hamburgers.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:51.73,0:02:54.34,Default,,0,0,0,,That guy and I would\Ngenetically be the same,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:54.34,0:02:56.78,Default,,0,0,0,,but we would be\Ncompletely different people.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:56.78,0:03:00.41,Default,,0,0,0,,The "Hamburger Spike" might be\Nmore short tempered than me...
Dialogue: 0,0:03:00.41,0:03:03.62,Default,,0,0,0,,Or might be the kind of guy\N that goes to church on Sundays.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:03.62,0:03:05.95,Default,,0,0,0,,He might be a violent bounty head...
Dialogue: 0,0:03:05.95,0:03:10.21,Default,,0,0,0,,Or a man that irons his\Nwhite shirts before wearing them.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:10.21,0:03:14.54,Default,,0,0,0,,At any rate, the "Hamburger Spike"\Nis a different person than me.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:14.54,0:03:18.66,Default,,0,0,0,,So in other words,\Nwhen choosing your food,
Dialogue: 0,0:03:18.66,0:03:20.97,Default,,0,0,0,,you have to think about it carefully.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:20.97,0:03:25.05,Default,,0,0,0,,I'll have the boiled lobster miso.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:25.05,0:03:26.43,Default,,0,0,0,,Very well.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:26.47,0:03:29.98,Default,,0,0,0,,"Fools Gold"
Dialogue: 0,0:03:30.60,0:03:34.27,Default,,0,0,0,,There's a lot to bonsai.\NIt's not as easy as just cutting.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:34.27,0:03:40.28,Default,,0,0,0,,Each bonsai has it's own personality...\Nand you have to let those live.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:40.28,0:03:44.95,Default,,0,0,0,,A foolish person will try to cut anything\Nand everything off just the same...
Dialogue: 0,0:03:44.95,0:03:49.00,Default,,0,0,0,,They just cut, and cut, and cut\Nthe parts that stick out.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:49.00,0:03:53.63,Default,,0,0,0,,Yet those parts that stick out are\Nit's personality...and it's originality.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:53.63,0:03:57.50,Default,,0,0,0,,People who can't even figure that out,\Ndon't have the right to hold scissors.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:57.50,0:04:01.34,Default,,0,0,0,,I feel sorry for the bonsai.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:01.34,0:04:03.68,Default,,0,0,0,,Do you know the basics of combat?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:11.48,0:04:14.98,Default,,0,0,0,,"Que Sera Sera"
Dialogue: 0,0:04:16.44,0:04:19.44,Default,,0,0,0,,I hate men with no thought.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:19.44,0:04:23.40,Default,,0,0,0,,But I hate men who force\Ntheir thought on others even more.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:23.40,0:04:26.28,Default,,0,0,0,,I hate men with pyorrhea too.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:26.28,0:04:29.29,Default,,0,0,0,,You can't even kiss a man\Nif his breath is bad.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:30.75,0:04:33.54,Default,,0,0,0,,I love dangerous men.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:33.54,0:04:36.67,Default,,0,0,0,,But...I have to think about the\Nones that are too dangerous.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:37.88,0:04:41.17,Default,,0,0,0,,I hate weak men.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:41.17,0:04:45.26,Default,,0,0,0,,I love men who know\Ntheir own weakness.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:45.26,0:04:48.68,Default,,0,0,0,,I love optimistic men.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:48.68,0:04:50.40,Default,,0,0,0,,I can't imagine trying to predict what happens
Dialogue: 0,0:04:50.40,0:04:53.20,Default,,0,0,0,,in advance and then living pessimistically...
Dialogue: 0,0:04:54.52,0:05:01.23,Default,,0,0,0,,Life, probably,no matter how it falls\Nturns out as it's going to turn out.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:01.23,0:05:03.90,Default,,0,0,0,,Yeah, because Ed is Ed.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:03.95,0:05:07.41,Default,,0,0,0,,"You Can't Always Get What You Want"
Dialogue: 0,0:05:18.13,0:05:19.38,Default,,0,0,0,,This is Ed.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:19.38,0:05:21.71,Default,,0,0,0,,Space is very vast.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:21.71,0:05:25.59,Default,,0,0,0,,Ed is traveling to find the truth of space.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:25.59,0:05:28.76,Default,,0,0,0,,When I walk barefoot,\Nit feels electric.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:28.76,0:05:33.68,Default,,0,0,0,,The network sea is so spacious,\Nthat there are lots of fish.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:33.68,0:05:37.90,Default,,0,0,0,,When I put something\Non my head, I get excited.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:37.90,0:05:40.65,Default,,0,0,0,,When I think there is a truth\Nand look for it, I can't find it...
Dialogue: 0,0:05:40.65,0:05:44.15,Default,,0,0,0,,But when I don't think there\Nis a truth, I can't find it either.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:44.15,0:05:49.87,Default,,0,0,0,,I can't get a hold of what I want,\Nbut I did get a hold of what I need.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:51.84,0:05:53.62,Default,,0,0,0,,You're too reliant on your eyes.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:53.62,0:05:55.12,Default,,0,0,0,,You're not a chameleon!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:55.12,0:05:56.79,Default,,0,0,0,,You can't see everything!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:56.79,0:06:00.29,Default,,0,0,0,,"Key of Life"
Dialogue: 0,0:06:00.92,0:06:03.67,Default,,0,0,0,,Humans live by their heart's beat.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:03.67,0:06:06.47,Default,,0,0,0,,A beat is a systematic repetition.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:06.47,0:06:08.18,Default,,0,0,0,,In other words, rhythm.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:08.18,0:06:11.93,Default,,0,0,0,,That's right. Whatever you are doing,\Nrhythm is of the most importance.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:11.93,0:06:12.97,Default,,0,0,0,,When walking...
Dialogue: 0,0:06:12.97,0:06:14.14,Default,,0,0,0,,When fighting...
Dialogue: 0,0:06:14.14,0:06:15.35,Default,,0,0,0,,When eating...
Dialogue: 0,0:06:15.35,0:06:16.52,Default,,0,0,0,,When making love...
Dialogue: 0,0:06:16.52,0:06:17.81,Default,,0,0,0,,When talking...
Dialogue: 0,0:06:17.81,0:06:20.06,Default,,0,0,0,,Rhythm is essential.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:20.06,0:06:23.57,Default,,0,0,0,,"Doggy Dog World"
Dialogue: 0,0:06:24.44,0:06:25.69,Default,,0,0,0,,Hey Ein.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:25.69,0:06:27.32,Default,,0,0,0,,Hey, hey, Ein.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:27.32,0:06:29.70,Default,,0,0,0,,Why are you so furry?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:29.70,0:06:33.87,Default,,0,0,0,,I know! Because\Nyou're sensitive to the cold!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:33.87,0:06:35.04,Default,,0,0,0,,Hey Ein.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:35.04,0:06:36.62,Default,,0,0,0,,In the first place, Ein.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:36.62,0:06:39.42,Default,,0,0,0,,Why aren't you laughing?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:39.42,0:06:42.79,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, that is because you're nihilistic.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:42.79,0:06:45.63,Default,,0,0,0,,Hey Ein.\NAfter all, Ein.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:45.63,0:06:48.51,Default,,0,0,0,,Why are you so happy?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:48.51,0:06:53.97,Default,,0,0,0,,That's right. Because\NEd is happy, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:53.97,0:06:55.88,Default,,0,0,0,,Charlie said,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:55.88,0:06:58.14,Default,,0,0,0,,"A hand must be a hand\Nin order for it to be washed."
Dialogue: 0,0:06:58.14,0:07:01.06,Default,,0,0,0,,"If you plan on taking, first give."
Dialogue: 0,0:07:01.06,0:07:02.94,Default,,0,0,0,,Now what does that mean?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:02.94,0:07:06.23,Default,,0,0,0,,Isn't Charlie saying, "Do it?"
Dialogue: 0,0:07:06.23,0:07:08.03,Default,,0,0,0,,Right?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:08.03,0:07:11.28,Default,,0,0,0,,You think Charlie Parker\Nwould quote Goethe's aphorism?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:11.28,0:07:14.83,Default,,0,0,0,,"Walk This Way"
Dialogue: 0,0:07:15.41,0:07:20.72,Default,,0,0,0,,"The greatest respect\Nthat a writer can give their readers..."
Dialogue: 0,0:07:20.72,0:07:24.34,Default,,0,0,0,,"... is to not write\Nanything that they expect."
Dialogue: 0,0:07:24.34,0:07:26.34,Default,,0,0,0,,That's what Goethe said.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:26.34,0:07:28.34,Default,,0,0,0,,He also said this:
Dialogue: 0,0:07:28.34,0:07:30.88,Default,,0,0,0,,"Whether it's a human work,\Nor a natural work..."
Dialogue: 0,0:07:30.88,0:07:37.97,Default,,0,0,0,,"...what we have to pay special\Nattention to is its original intent."
Dialogue: 0,0:07:37.97,0:07:40.98,Default,,0,0,0,,That guy says some good things...
Dialogue: 0,0:07:40.98,0:07:43.10,Default,,0,0,0,,Who would have thought that I would
Dialogue: 0,0:07:43.10,0:07:46.15,Default,,0,0,0,,quit being a cop and\Nbecome a bounty hunter?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:46.15,0:07:48.64,Default,,0,0,0,,All my old friends are surprised...
Dialogue: 0,0:07:48.64,0:07:51.95,Default,,0,0,0,,Saying, "You totally\Nbetrayed my expectations."
Dialogue: 0,0:07:51.95,0:07:52.74,Default,,0,0,0,,But that's fine.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:52.74,0:07:56.37,Default,,0,0,0,,I want to do something that\Nnobody else would think of.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:56.37,0:08:00.25,Default,,0,0,0,,Seeing things you've never seen...\NHearing stories you've never heard...
Dialogue: 0,0:08:00.25,0:08:04.63,Default,,0,0,0,,My comrades enjoy that quite a bit.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:04.63,0:08:08.13,Default,,0,0,0,,"A Natural Woman"
Dialogue: 0,0:08:08.84,0:08:10.97,Default,,0,0,0,,I hate simplicity.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:10.97,0:08:13.76,Default,,0,0,0,,I hate overcleanliness too
Dialogue: 0,0:08:13.76,0:08:15.48,Default,,0,0,0,,Being at least a little dirty,
Dialogue: 0,0:08:15.49,0:08:19.27,Default,,0,0,0,,makes your room and\Nthe world easier to live in.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:19.27,0:08:21.52,Default,,0,0,0,,They say that "White\Nskin hides seven blemishes,"
Dialogue: 0,0:08:21.52,0:08:23.77,Default,,0,0,0,,but I hate hiding.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:23.77,0:08:24.85,Default,,0,0,0,,Stains...
Dialogue: 0,0:08:24.85,0:08:26.36,Default,,0,0,0,,Freckles...
Dialogue: 0,0:08:26.36,0:08:27.77,Default,,0,0,0,,What's wrong with that?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:27.77,0:08:30.40,Default,,0,0,0,,If everyone had the\Nsame skin, same face...
Dialogue: 0,0:08:30.40,0:08:33.87,Default,,0,0,0,,you couldn't tell who you were.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:33.87,0:08:36.74,Default,,0,0,0,,I don't know myself as it is.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:36.74,0:08:41.20,Default,,0,0,0,,That's why...\NI can't erase the clues.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:41.20,0:08:44.62,Default,,0,0,0,,They're all guideposts to myself, you see.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:44.62,0:08:47.21,Default,,0,0,0,,Because you can't tell\Nwomen from their looks...
Dialogue: 0,0:08:48.92,0:08:52.42,Default,,0,0,0,,"Instant Karma!"
Dialogue: 0,0:08:54.93,0:08:56.97,Default,,0,0,0,,Laughing Bull spoke:
Dialogue: 0,0:08:56.97,0:09:01.14,Default,,0,0,0,,"Swimming bird, do you know\Nwhat your body is made from?"
Dialogue: 0,0:09:01.14,0:09:02.35,Default,,0,0,0,,I spoke:
Dialogue: 0,0:09:02.35,0:09:03.78,Default,,0,0,0,,"I don't know."
Dialogue: 0,0:09:03.78,0:09:07.15,Default,,0,0,0,,"Probably some bird droppings\Nthat's rolling around somewhere."
Dialogue: 0,0:09:07.15,0:09:08.48,Default,,0,0,0,,Bull spoke:
Dialogue: 0,0:09:08.48,0:09:12.78,Default,,0,0,0,,"Swimming bird, do you know\Nwhat your soul is made from?"
Dialogue: 0,0:09:12.78,0:09:14.03,Default,,0,0,0,,I spoke:
Dialogue: 0,0:09:14.03,0:09:15.34,Default,,0,0,0,,"I don't know."
Dialogue: 0,0:09:15.33,0:09:18.62,Default,,0,0,0,,"Probably some cotton dust\Nthat's rolling around somewhere."
Dialogue: 0,0:09:18.62,0:09:20.03,Default,,0,0,0,,Bull spoke:
Dialogue: 0,0:09:20.03,0:09:23.04,Default,,0,0,0,,"That answer is wrong; yet right."
Dialogue: 0,0:09:23.04,0:09:28.25,Default,,0,0,0,,"Your body is connected with\Nthe universe; yet it is not."
Dialogue: 0,0:09:28.25,0:09:33.21,Default,,0,0,0,,"Your soul includes the entire\Nuniverse; yet it does not."
Dialogue: 0,0:09:33.21,0:09:36.72,Default,,0,0,0,,"That is for me...\Nand for everyone."
Dialogue: 0,0:09:36.72,0:09:40.56,Default,,0,0,0,,"If you hate someone,\Nyou hate yourself."
Dialogue: 0,0:09:40.56,0:09:45.06,Default,,0,0,0,,"If you love someone,\Nyou love yourself."
Dialogue: 0,0:09:45.06,0:09:46.98,Default,,0,0,0,,I spoke:
Dialogue: 0,0:09:46.98,0:09:49.81,Default,,0,0,0,,"I don't feel anything towards anyone."
Dialogue: 0,0:09:49.81,0:09:51.65,Default,,0,0,0,,Bull spoke:
Dialogue: 0,0:09:51.65,0:09:55.53,Default,,0,0,0,,"That is... the greatest\Nmisfortune on this earth."
Dialogue: 0,0:10:10.34,0:10:13.84,Default,,0,0,0,,"Sugar Mountain"
Dialogue: 0,0:10:14.75,0:10:17.01,Default,,0,0,0,,If you give a baby only sweet things...
Dialogue: 0,0:10:17.01,0:10:19.29,Default,,0,0,0,,They say it'll only\Nwant that and wont
Dialogue: 0,0:10:19.29,0:10:22.01,Default,,0,0,0,,eat the nutritious\Nfoods that are vital.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:22.01,0:10:26.02,Default,,0,0,0,,Things like sugar candy\Nare the poison after all.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:26.02,0:10:28.52,Default,,0,0,0,,Now, it's not like I'm\Nonly talking about food.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:28.52,0:10:31.11,Default,,0,0,0,,The world is is full of sugar candy.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:31.11,0:10:32.85,Default,,0,0,0,,If you only watch stuff like that,
Dialogue: 0,0:10:32.85,0:10:36.11,Default,,0,0,0,,your brain will rot\Nand become yogurt.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:36.19,0:10:40.20,Default,,0,0,0,,"Chain of Fools"
Dialogue: 0,0:10:36.99,0:10:40.20,Default,,0,0,0,,Well you see, there's a lot to cooking.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:40.20,0:10:42.83,Default,,0,0,0,,It's not as easy as\Njust randomly adding flavor.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:42.83,0:10:45.11,Default,,0,0,0,,A foolish person will\Nput in too much flavor
Dialogue: 0,0:10:45.11,0:10:47.44,Default,,0,0,0,,and make a dish\Nthat you can't tell
Dialogue: 0,0:10:47.44,0:10:49.37,Default,,0,0,0,,whether it's beef or chicken.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:49.37,0:10:53.29,Default,,0,0,0,,Those kind of people...\Nshouldn't hold a wok.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:53.29,0:10:55.42,Default,,0,0,0,,The original flavor of the ingredients...
Dialogue: 0,0:10:55.42,0:10:56.53,Default,,0,0,0,,In other words...
Dialogue: 0,0:10:56.53,0:11:00.55,Default,,0,0,0,,If it's beef, then you have\Nto let the originality of the beef live.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:00.55,0:11:03.35,Default,,0,0,0,,Otherwise the beef will be sad.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:03.76,0:11:06.14,Default,,0,0,0,,Those who don't work\Nhave no right to eat.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:06.14,0:11:09.69,Default,,0,0,0,,Get you own food.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:09.69,0:11:11.27,Default,,0,0,0,,I don't count.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:11.27,0:11:13.90,Default,,0,0,0,,Women are great\Njust by staying alive.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:13.98,0:11:17.49,Default,,0,0,0,,"Do It Yourself"
Dialogue: 0,0:11:17.61,0:11:22.16,Default,,0,0,0,,"Don't rely on others\Nand do things yourself."
Dialogue: 0,0:11:22.16,0:11:24.37,Default,,0,0,0,,I don't know who taught it to me,
Dialogue: 0,0:11:24.37,0:11:27.54,Default,,0,0,0,,but for some time\NI've been believing in that.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:27.54,0:11:30.21,Default,,0,0,0,,It's not that big of a deal though.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:30.21,0:11:34.42,Default,,0,0,0,,I wouldn't want to be relied upon\Nand not be able to come through.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:34.42,0:11:39.97,Default,,0,0,0,,And even if I did I'll wonder,\N"Was it really for their sake?" and such.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:39.97,0:11:46.14,Default,,0,0,0,,In the end...\Nyou have to grab your own luck.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:46.14,0:11:51.02,Default,,0,0,0,,Women will quickly betray you,\Nbut men live by duty.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:51.02,0:11:52.60,Default,,0,0,0,,Duty, huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:52.60,0:11:55.02,Default,,0,0,0,,That's what I'd like to believe.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:55.02,0:11:58.53,Default,,0,0,0,,"If 6 Was 9"
Dialogue: 0,0:12:00.11,0:12:02.28,Default,,0,0,0,,Doubting everything that you take on...
Dialogue: 0,0:12:02.28,0:12:03.91,Default,,0,0,0,,That is very important.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:03.91,0:12:06.20,Default,,0,0,0,,Information is only information, after all.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:06.20,0:12:09.54,Default,,0,0,0,,If you think what they say on\NTV is the truth, you're gravely mistaken.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:09.54,0:12:11.53,Default,,0,0,0,,Open your own eyes, clear out your ears,
Dialogue: 0,0:12:11.53,0:12:14.00,Default,,0,0,0,,and look and listen to the world...
Dialogue: 0,0:12:14.00,0:12:17.05,Default,,0,0,0,,And think using your own brain.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:17.05,0:12:19.26,Default,,0,0,0,,After you've doubted everything,
Dialogue: 0,0:12:19.26,0:12:22.47,Default,,0,0,0,,there is a possibility of\Nsomething real to believe in.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:22.47,0:12:23.44,Default,,0,0,0,,That's right.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:23.44,0:12:27.26,Default,,0,0,0,,To believe in something, doubt everything.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:27.26,0:12:29.98,Default,,0,0,0,,It's not the question of that being hard.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:29.98,0:12:31.48,Default,,0,0,0,,It's impossible!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:31.48,0:12:34.85,Default,,0,0,0,,It's like trying to play baseball\Nwithout holding a bat.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:34.85,0:12:36.86,Default,,0,0,0,,Hey, Spike!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:36.86,0:12:39.69,Default,,0,0,0,,That's the kind of thing I like.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:39.69,0:12:43.20,Default,,0,0,0,,"Amazing Grace"
Dialogue: 0,0:12:44.41,0:12:46.95,Default,,0,0,0,,The good part about bounty hunting...
Dialogue: 0,0:12:46.95,0:12:48.74,Default,,0,0,0,,is that there are no rules.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:48.74,0:12:50.39,Default,,0,0,0,,To capture the bounty...
Dialogue: 0,0:12:50.39,0:12:54.92,Default,,0,0,0,,there is no written\N"Do This" in existence.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:54.92,0:12:56.50,Default,,0,0,0,,But if you do\Nwhatever you want,
Dialogue: 0,0:12:56.50,0:12:58.80,Default,,0,0,0,,they'll start complaining...
Dialogue: 0,0:12:58.80,0:13:01.80,Default,,0,0,0,,Or get mad and say\Nthat it's against the rules.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:01.80,0:13:06.39,Default,,0,0,0,,They're supposed to be living\Nby following this world's rules...
Dialogue: 0,0:13:06.39,0:13:09.93,Default,,0,0,0,,But who made those rules?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:09.93,0:13:13.77,Default,,0,0,0,,It's not like we were born to obey somebody...
Dialogue: 0,0:13:13.77,0:13:17.69,Default,,0,0,0,,Whether threatened of bribed,\Nour souls can't be sold.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:17.69,0:13:22.28,Default,,0,0,0,,Unfortunately, the free-lance soul is an antique.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:22.28,0:13:24.82,Default,,0,0,0,,What?\NAnd that heart?
Dialogue: 0,0:13:24.82,0:13:28.91,Default,,0,0,0,,It's too expensive for money to buy.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:28.91,0:13:32.79,Default,,0,0,0,,Lesson, lesson.\NIf we meet a stranger, follow him!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:32.79,0:13:37.96,Default,,0,0,0,,"My Favorite Things"
Dialogue: 0,0:13:39.79,0:13:43.59,Default,,0,0,0,,Ed has not had any sufferings yet.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:43.59,0:13:49.47,Default,,0,0,0,,Perhaps I might have,\Nbut I don't remember at all.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:49.47,0:13:55.98,Default,,0,0,0,,If you ask why, it's because\NI only do things that look fun...
Dialogue: 0,0:13:55.98,0:13:58.23,Default,,0,0,0,,And even with boring things,
Dialogue: 0,0:13:58.23,0:14:00.90,Default,,0,0,0,,I find something a little\Nfun in them and get excited.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:00.90,0:14:05.11,Default,,0,0,0,,But if it's still boring, I go to sleep.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:05.11,0:14:08.49,Default,,0,0,0,,When I'm asleep,\Nit's fun rolling around dreaming.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:08.49,0:14:09.57,Default,,0,0,0,,The end.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:13.37,0:14:15.87,Default,,0,0,0,,I didn't put strength anywhere.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:15.87,0:14:18.92,Default,,0,0,0,,I just used your wasted strength.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:18.92,0:14:21.79,Default,,0,0,0,,You have to control the flow of strength.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:21.79,0:14:25.18,Default,,0,0,0,,In order to do that, loosen yourself
Dialogue: 0,0:14:25.18,0:14:27.51,Default,,0,0,0,,so you can counter\Nany type of movement and...
Dialogue: 0,0:14:27.51,0:14:29.09,Default,,0,0,0,,That's right.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:29.09,0:14:31.43,Default,,0,0,0,,Be like water.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:31.43,0:14:34.93,Default,,0,0,0,,"Unfinished Sympathy"
Dialogue: 0,0:14:36.02,0:14:38.56,Default,,0,0,0,,Bruce Lee was said to say this:
Dialogue: 0,0:14:38.56,0:14:41.44,Default,,0,0,0,,"Empty your mind and throw away..."
Dialogue: 0,0:14:41.44,0:14:44.15,Default,,0,0,0,,"...any form or shape and be like water."
Dialogue: 0,0:14:44.15,0:14:47.49,Default,,0,0,0,,"If you put water in a cup,\Nthe water becomes the cup."
Dialogue: 0,0:14:47.49,0:14:51.57,Default,,0,0,0,,"If you put water in a tea pot,\Nthe water becomes the tea pot."
Dialogue: 0,0:14:51.57,0:14:55.62,Default,,0,0,0,,"Water can flow,\Nor it can violently crash."
Dialogue: 0,0:14:55.62,0:14:59.58,Default,,0,0,0,,"That is why, my friend, be like water."
Dialogue: 0,0:15:01.21,0:15:04.59,Default,,0,0,0,,As expected, my heart's\Nmentor speaks differently.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:04.59,0:15:07.05,Default,,0,0,0,,He also said this:
Dialogue: 0,0:15:07.05,0:15:09.95,Default,,0,0,0,,"What I am teaching is not self-defense..."
Dialogue: 0,0:15:09.95,0:15:13.18,Default,,0,0,0,,"...or how to defeat opponents\Nor anything like that..."
Dialogue: 0,0:15:13.18,0:15:19.10,Default,,0,0,0,,"But rather, how to express\Nyourself through your movements."
Dialogue: 0,0:15:19.10,0:15:22.98,Default,,0,0,0,,"Whether that is anger,\Ndetermination, or whatever."
Dialogue: 0,0:15:22.98,0:15:23.87,Default,,0,0,0,,"In other words..."
Dialogue: 0,0:15:23.87,0:15:29.53,Default,,0,0,0,,"...a method of expression using\Nthe human body with combat."
Dialogue: 0,0:15:29.53,0:15:31.62,Default,,0,0,0,,You can tell that Bruce Lee\Nwasn't just some movie star
Dialogue: 0,0:15:31.62,0:15:35.12,Default,,0,0,0,,or just some martial artist, can't you?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:35.73,0:15:37.50,Default,,0,0,0,,The chain is long...
Dialogue: 0,0:15:37.50,0:15:39.50,Default,,0,0,0,,Is it the "Way of the Dragon" model?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:39.50,0:15:40.79,Default,,0,0,0,,Oh, you can tell?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:40.79,0:15:44.29,Default,,0,0,0,,"Public Pressure"
Dialogue: 0,0:15:45.21,0:15:50.51,Default,,0,0,0,,If there is a God in this world,\NI'd like to ask one wish.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:50.51,0:15:55.60,Default,,0,0,0,,Divine retribution to all\Nthose who take freedom away.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:55.60,0:15:59.10,Default,,0,0,0,,"Whole Lotta Love"
Dialogue: 0,0:16:00.19,0:16:01.56,Default,,0,0,0,,I sometimes think...
Dialogue: 0,0:16:01.56,0:16:03.79,Default,,0,0,0,,I miss out on a\Nlot with this personality.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:03.79,0:16:05.72,Default,,0,0,0,,I sometimes think so...
Dialogue: 0,0:16:05.72,0:16:09.15,Default,,0,0,0,,that this way all the\Ngood men will run away.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:09.15,0:16:13.95,Default,,0,0,0,,Well, this is who I am\Nso it can't be helped...
Dialogue: 0,0:16:13.95,0:16:16.00,Default,,0,0,0,,If I act like someone else saying,
Dialogue: 0,0:16:16.00,0:16:19.12,Default,,0,0,0,,"Even though I look like this\NI'm really a home maker!"
Dialogue: 0,0:16:19.12,0:16:22.29,Default,,0,0,0,,Or whatever...\NEven if it did get anywhere good...
Dialogue: 0,0:16:22.29,0:16:24.29,Default,,0,0,0,,In the end... \Nhardship...No...
Dialogue: 0,0:16:24.29,0:16:27.25,Default,,0,0,0,,Only regret will come.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:27.25,0:16:32.22,Default,,0,0,0,,Me... It's got to be someone\Nthat will like me for myself.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:32.22,0:16:35.85,Default,,0,0,0,,Well, I think it'll be tough being with me but...
Dialogue: 0,0:16:35.85,0:16:40.09,Default,,0,0,0,,There's probably a man unlucky\Nenough in the universe though.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:40.56,0:16:44.56,Default,,0,0,0,,Yeah, the blues\Nharp is great. It's great.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:44.56,0:16:47.07,Default,,0,0,0,,Weren't you a jazz fan?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:47.07,0:16:48.46,Default,,0,0,0,,Don't be stupid!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:48.46,0:16:53.32,Default,,0,0,0,,I was listening to warbling\Nwhile I was drinking my mom's milk.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:53.32,0:16:55.20,Default,,0,0,0,,Well you were a clever kid.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:55.20,0:16:58.70,Default,,0,0,0,,"Wild Style"
Dialogue: 0,0:17:00.25,0:17:05.79,Default,,0,0,0,,Over a century ago there was\Na sax player called Charlie Parker.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:05.79,0:17:10.26,Default,,0,0,0,,He seemed to be the first man\Nto play without using sheet music.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:10.26,0:17:11.34,Default,,0,0,0,,In other words,
Dialogue: 0,0:17:11.34,0:17:14.21,Default,,0,0,0,,he was tired of playing the same thing
Dialogue: 0,0:17:14.21,0:17:19.22,Default,,0,0,0,,and started ad-libbing\Nand playing in his own style.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:19.22,0:17:24.23,Default,,0,0,0,,The music that he started\Neventually came to be called Bebop.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:24.23,0:17:26.15,Default,,0,0,0,,That's right.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:26.15,0:17:29.73,Default,,0,0,0,,That's the origin of this ship's name.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:29.73,0:17:33.24,Default,,0,0,0,,"Daydream Believer"
Dialogue: 0,0:17:35.78,0:17:41.45,Default,,0,0,0,,We all sleep while we wake up\Nand wake up while we sleep.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:41.45,0:17:43.58,Default,,0,0,0,,Is the past reality?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:43.58,0:17:46.21,Default,,0,0,0,,Are memories the truth?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:46.21,0:17:49.88,Default,,0,0,0,,Where are dreams, dreams?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:49.88,0:17:53.88,Default,,0,0,0,,The dreams we dream while asleep...\Nthe drams we dream while awake.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:53.88,0:17:56.51,Default,,0,0,0,,They're both the same.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:56.51,0:17:59.72,Default,,0,0,0,,The people that say they don't\Ndream only don't remember.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:59.72,0:18:03.43,Default,,0,0,0,,The people with no dreams\Nhave only yet to notice them.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:03.43,0:18:05.10,Default,,0,0,0,,They're cowards.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:05.10,0:18:09.40,Default,,0,0,0,,They want to see them, but they're\Nmerely forcing themselves not to.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:09.40,0:18:12.94,Default,,0,0,0,,"Hang on to Yourself"
Dialogue: 0,0:18:10.40,0:18:13.65,Default,,0,0,0,,And this is just an illusion.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:13.65,0:18:15.56,Default,,0,0,0,,Controlled by an unseen hand,
Dialogue: 0,0:18:15.56,0:18:18.99,Default,,0,0,0,,the truth is still\Ncovered by a thick veil.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:18.99,0:18:25.08,Default,,0,0,0,,But it quietly, like the\Nmoons of Titan, secretly exists.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:25.08,0:18:29.83,Default,,0,0,0,,Eventually showing itself\Nafter the sand storm clears.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:29.83,0:18:33.34,Default,,0,0,0,,"Look Back In Anger"
Dialogue: 0,0:18:30.88,0:18:32.40,Default,,0,0,0,,So...
Dialogue: 0,0:18:32.40,0:18:36.63,Default,,0,0,0,,Let's stop getting angry\Nover such simple pleasures.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:36.63,0:18:40.43,Default,,0,0,0,,This isn't a joke.\NNor is it fiction.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:40.43,0:18:44.68,Default,,0,0,0,,Or... Have I been\Nseeing a bad dream?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:44.68,0:18:48.19,Default,,0,0,0,,"Tangled Up In Blue"
Dialogue: 0,0:18:48.87,0:18:50.89,Default,,0,0,0,,A blues man somewhere...
Dialogue: 0,0:18:50.89,0:18:54.32,Default,,0,0,0,,was said to say this after\Nbeing asked the definition of blues...
Dialogue: 0,0:18:54.32,0:18:56.01,Default,,0,0,0,,"Blues is..."
Dialogue: 0,0:18:56.01,0:18:59.19,Default,,0,0,0,,"...singing about some kind\Nof trouble that can't be helped."
Dialogue: 0,0:18:59.20,0:19:02.70,Default,,0,0,0,,"It's All Over Now, Baby Blue"
Dialogue: 0,0:19:41.61,0:19:44.58,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H000000&\3c&HFFFFFF&\4c&HFFFFFF&}Sora wo ubaware  Ashita ga ware\N{\c&HFFFFFF&\3c&H000000&\4c&H000000&}The sky is taken. Tomorrow is broken.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:44.58,0:19:47.29,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H000000&\3c&HFFFFFF&\4c&HFFFFFF&}Kokoro mushibamu yami ga umare\N{\c&HFFFFFF&\3c&H000000&\4c&H000000&}A darkness that eats into hearts is born.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:47.29,0:19:49.79,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H000000&\3c&HFFFFFF&\4c&HFFFFFF&}Yume wa kare  Fuan ni nare\N{\c&HFFFFFF&\3c&H000000&\4c&H000000&}Dreams are withered. All are uneased.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:49.79,0:19:53.46,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H000000&\3c&HFFFFFF&\4c&HFFFFFF&}Ah  Sora no yukue wo shiru no wa dare?\N{\c&HFFFFFF&\3c&H000000&\4c&H000000&}Ah, who knows the whereabouts of the sky?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:53.46,0:19:55.04,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H000000&\3c&HFFFFFF&\4c&HFFFFFF&}Oshiete okure\N{\c&HFFFFFF&\3c&H000000&\4c&H000000&}Tell me.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:55.04,0:19:58.46,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H000000&\3c&HFFFFFF&\4c&HFFFFFF&}Yukiba ushinau tori to kumo to hoshi to ore\N{\c&HFFFFFF&\3c&H000000&\4c&H000000&}The birds, the clouds, and I\N lose a place to go.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:58.46,0:20:00.76,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H000000&\3c&HFFFFFF&\4c&HFFFFFF&}Ichinichi no sakai ga kie\N{\c&HFFFFFF&\3c&H000000&\4c&H000000&}The borders of the day disappear.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:00.76,0:20:04.05,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H000000&\3c&HFFFFFF&\4c&HFFFFFF&}Suteta tokei  Korogaru machi wa grey\N{\c&HFFFFFF&\3c&H000000&\4c&H000000&}Watches are thrown away.\NTowns are always grey.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:04.05,0:20:05.97,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H000000&\3c&HFFFFFF&\4c&HFFFFFF&}Noboru yane no teppen\N{\c&HFFFFFF&\3c&H000000&\4c&H000000&}Climbed to the top of the roof...
Dialogue: 0,0:20:05.97,0:20:08.64,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H000000&\3c&HFFFFFF&\4c&HFFFFFF&}Imagination de hikou kunren\N{\c&HFFFFFF&\3c&H000000&\4c&H000000&}...practiced flying with my imagination.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:08.64,0:20:11.39,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H000000&\3c&HFFFFFF&\4c&HFFFFFF&}Nani mo osorezu tobu ore ni miren\N{\c&HFFFFFF&\3c&H000000&\4c&H000000&}Regret the loss of when I flew without fear.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:11.39,0:20:14.31,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H000000&\3c&HFFFFFF&\4c&HFFFFFF&}Karada no naka de kodama suru siren\N{\c&HFFFFFF&\3c&H000000&\4c&H000000&}A siren that echos within my body.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:14.31,0:20:16.61,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H000000&\3c&HFFFFFF&\4c&HFFFFFF&}Subete nagedashita hito wo mi\N{\c&HFFFFFF&\3c&H000000&\4c&H000000&}Look at the people who gave up everything.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:16.61,0:20:20.03,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H000000&\3c&HFFFFFF&\4c&HFFFFFF&}Asu wa waga mi  Miushinaisou na tomi\N{\c&HFFFFFF&\3c&H000000&\4c&H000000&}It may happen to me tomorrow.\NWealth is about to disappear.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:20.03,0:20:22.11,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H000000&\3c&HFFFFFF&\4c&HFFFFFF&}Komiageru namida nomi\N{\c&HFFFFFF&\3c&H000000&\4c&H000000&}Keep down the rising tears.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:22.11,0:20:26.08,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H000000&\3c&HFFFFFF&\4c&HFFFFFF&}Mou hirakitakunai kono hitomi\N{\c&HFFFFFF&\3c&H000000&\4c&H000000&}Don't want to open these eyes anymore.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:26.08,0:20:30.50,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H000000&\3c&HFFFFFF&\4c&HFFFFFF&}Mabuta wo tojita toki ni mieta hikari\N{\c&HFFFFFF&\3c&H000000&\4c&H000000&}The light I saw when I closed my eyelids...
Dialogue: 0,0:20:30.50,0:20:35.04,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H000000&\3c&HFFFFFF&\4c&HFFFFFF&}Sagashiteru ore wa hitori  Hitori\N{\c&HFFFFFF&\3c&H000000&\4c&H000000&}I am looking for it alone. Alone.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:56.48,0:20:59.44,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H000000&\3c&HFFFFFF&\4c&HFFFFFF&}Usureteyuku shinjitsu no rinkaku\N{\c&HFFFFFF&\3c&H000000&\4c&H000000&}The thinning outlines of truth...
Dialogue: 0,0:20:59.44,0:21:02.95,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H000000&\3c&HFFFFFF&\4c&HFFFFFF&}Ikaku shiau fuan to kibou no tatakai wa gokaku\N{\c&HFFFFFF&\3c&H000000&\4c&H000000&}The fight between the threatning\Nuneasiness and hope is even.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:02.95,0:21:05.37,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H000000&\3c&HFFFFFF&\4c&HFFFFFF&}Minukenai Tokyo no sakkaku\N{\c&HFFFFFF&\3c&H000000&\4c&H000000&}The illusion of Tokyo can't be seen through.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:05.37,0:21:07.16,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H000000&\3c&HFFFFFF&\4c&HFFFFFF&}Damasarerya shikkaku\N{\c&HFFFFFF&\3c&H000000&\4c&H000000&}If you're fooled, you're lost.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:07.16,0:21:09.70,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H000000&\3c&HFFFFFF&\4c&HFFFFFF&}Kono furubita hane wa mukashi mitaku\N{\c&HFFFFFF&\3c&H000000&\4c&H000000&}These old wings like long ago...
Dialogue: 0,0:21:09.70,0:21:13.25,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H000000&\3c&HFFFFFF&\4c&HFFFFFF&}Iukoto kikuka mattaku wakarazu kuttaku\N{\c&HFFFFFF&\3c&H000000&\4c&H000000&}...worried and don't know that they'll work.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:13.25,0:21:15.75,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H000000&\3c&HFFFFFF&\4c&HFFFFFF&}Demo chuu wo mau yume wa idaku\N{\c&HFFFFFF&\3c&H000000&\4c&H000000&}But I embrace the dream of dancing in the air.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:15.75,0:21:18.09,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H000000&\3c&HFFFFFF&\4c&HFFFFFF&}Sono ikikata wa nitaku\N{\c&HFFFFFF&\3c&H000000&\4c&H000000&}That life has two possibilities.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:18.09,0:21:21.46,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H000000&\3c&HFFFFFF&\4c&HFFFFFF&}Ah  Sora ga kininari nemurenai\N{\c&HFFFFFF&\3c&H000000&\4c&H000000&}Ah, I'm worried about the sky and can't sleep.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:21.46,0:21:23.63,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H000000&\3c&HFFFFFF&\4c&HFFFFFF&}Nemuru furi mo dekinai\N{\c&HFFFFFF&\3c&H000000&\4c&H000000&}I can't even pretend to sleep.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:23.63,0:21:26.34,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H000000&\3c&HFFFFFF&\4c&HFFFFFF&}Kore ijou  Hontou no kotoba\N{\c&HFFFFFF&\3c&H000000&\4c&H000000&}Not any more. The real word.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:26.34,0:21:29.14,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H000000&\3c&HFFFFFF&\4c&HFFFFFF&}Hito makase ni wa dekinai\N{\c&HFFFFFF&\3c&H000000&\4c&H000000&}I can't leave it up to other people.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:29.14,0:21:31.85,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H000000&\3c&HFFFFFF&\4c&HFFFFFF&}Mittsu kazoe miagetara\N{\c&HFFFFFF&\3c&H000000&\4c&H000000&}After I count to three and look up...
Dialogue: 0,0:21:31.85,0:21:34.44,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H000000&\3c&HFFFFFF&\4c&HFFFFFF&}Iki ga tomaru you na oozora\N{\c&HFFFFFF&\3c&H000000&\4c&H000000&}A great sky that takes your breath away.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:34.44,0:21:36.06,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H000000&\3c&HFFFFFF&\4c&HFFFFFF&}Moto ni modore\N{\c&HFFFFFF&\3c&H000000&\4c&H000000&}Please come back.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:36.06,0:21:37.11,Default - Left,,0,0,0,,{\c&H000000&\3c&HFFFFFF&\4c&HFFFFFF&}Hitotsu\N{\c&HFFFFFF&\3c&H000000&\4c&H000000&}One
Dialogue: 0,0:21:37.11,0:21:38.06,Default - Left,,0,0,0,,{\c&H000000&\3c&HFFFFFF&\4c&HFFFFFF&}Hitotsu, futatsu\N{\c&HFFFFFF&\3c&H000000&\4c&H000000&}One, two
Dialogue: 0,0:21:38.06,0:21:38.57,Default - Left,,0,0,0,,{\c&H000000&\3c&HFFFFFF&\4c&HFFFFFF&}Hitotsu, futatsu, mittsu\N{\c&HFFFFFF&\3c&H000000&\4c&H000000&}One, two, three
Dialogue: 0,0:21:38.57,0:21:42.03,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H000000&\3c&HFFFFFF&\4c&HFFFFFF&}Itsu no hi ka ano toki no sora torimodoshi\N{\c&HFFFFFF&\3c&H000000&\4c&H000000&}One day the sky from that time will be taken back.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:42.03,0:21:45.15,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H000000&\3c&HFFFFFF&\4c&HFFFFFF&}Mayoeru mono doushi Wa ni nari yodoushi\N{\c&HFFFFFF&\3c&H000000&\4c&H000000&}All those who are lost form a ring all night.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:45.15,0:21:47.45,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H000000&\3c&HFFFFFF&\4c&HFFFFFF&}Katariai wasurerarenai\N{\c&HFFFFFF&\3c&H000000&\4c&H000000&}We talk and can't forget.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:47.45,0:21:52.08,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H000000&\3c&HFFFFFF&\4c&HFFFFFF&}Utsumuita hibi wo warai tobashitai\N{\c&HFFFFFF&\3c&H000000&\4c&H000000&}We want to laugh off the upside down days.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:52.08,0:21:57.08,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H000000&\3c&HFFFFFF&\4c&HFFFFFF&}Umarete hajimete mita senmei na kibou\N{\c&HFFFFFF&\3c&H000000&\4c&H000000&}A vivid hope that I've never seen before.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:57.08,0:22:02.67,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H000000&\3c&HFFFFFF&\4c&HFFFFFF&}Sore wa tsuyoi kokoro ni himerareta yabou\N{\c&HFFFFFF&\3c&H000000&\4c&H000000&}That is an ambition hidden in a strong heart.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:02.67,0:22:08.01,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H000000&\3c&HFFFFFF&\4c&HFFFFFF&}Mugen ni hirogaru aoi sekai he toubou\N{\c&HFFFFFF&\3c&H000000&\4c&H000000&}Let's run away to the boundless blue world.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:08.01,0:22:13.77,Default,,0,0,0,,{\c&H000000&\3c&HFFFFFF&\4c&HFFFFFF&}Ima, hontou no sora he tobou\N{\c&HFFFFFF&\3c&H000000&\4c&H000000&}Now, let's fly to the real sky.
